# Frontend design system

| Role | Hex |
|---|---|
| Primary header | `#1B2A4A` |
| Secondary header | `#3D4C6C` |
| Accent (charts/highlights) | `#17A398` |
| Input border/accent | `#7B93A8` |
| Page background | `#FAF7F0` |
| Body text | `#1A1A1A` |
| Validation pass | `#6B9E78` |
| Validation fail | `#C1666B` |
| Threshold lines only | `#C9A227` |

Font: `'Open Sans', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif`

## Formatting

- Currency: no decimals except tax-detail lines (`$#,##0` vs `$#,##0.00`)
- Rates: one decimal for inputs (`10.0%`), two for computed effective rates (`12.31%`)

## Charts (Chart.js)

- Teal = nominal; slate = real/inflation-adjusted; amber = threshold lines only — same meaning on every chart
- Strip default Chart.js borders/shadows; minimal gridlines; typography matches the page
- Re-render from fresh arrays every calc — no Excel-style named-range binding concerns

Illustrative assumptions (C-CPI-U proxy, SSA wage-base vs CPI, flat state tax) must be labeled honestly in UI copy.
